Wed Apr 28 10:48:23 1999    <reddy@MAGNOLIA>

	* ThreeDPanel.c (ThreeDPanelCreateRenderWidgets): remove the
 	slider widgets for setting the near and far planes in the Render
 	Panel. These settings are now controlled automatically.

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetKeypress): make the grab_pointer
 	parameter be GrabModeAsync not GrabModeSync otherwise we would
 	never receive mouse up/down events while keyboard was grabbed
 	(i.e. you couldn't do slide operations with SHIFT down).
	(Distance3D): calculate distance between 2 3D points that are
 	specified as 6 doubles - currently just a wrapper to Distance().

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetSetClipPlanes): [new func] attempts
 	to automatically set the near and far clipping planes based upon
 	the bounding box of the current visible tile list. This is done by
 	setting the far plane to the furthest point of visible geometry,
 	and then setting the near plane so that we keep the ratio near:far
 	within a prescribed range to elimiate flimmering. We also impose a
 	minimum value on the near plane so that if the near plane is set
 	to less than this value, then we threshold it and then push out
 	the far plane as far as we can based upon the prescribed near:far
 	ratio.
	
	* Visible.c (VisibleClear): initialise the geo_bbox field to be
 	invalid by default (no bounding box defined)
	(GenVisibleList1): Added a new parameter to the function,
 	geo_bbox, which gets updated to contain the bounding box of all
 	visible tiles. Inside this function we now compute the LVCS
 	bounding box for the set of visible tiles in this geo, and then we
 	convert this to GCC when done and then take the largest enclosing
 	GCC bounding box between this and the previous bbox for the
 	visible list (i.e. from any other geos)
	(GenVisibleList): update the geo_bbox field of the VisibleList
 	structure with the bounding box of the entire visible list

	* Visible.h: created a new structure GeoBBox to hold a full
 	geocentric bounding box. Added a geo_bbox field to the VisibleList
 	structure in order to record the bounding box of all visible
 	tiles.

