Sat Mar 27 14:49:48 1999  Martin Reddy  <reddy@MAGNOLIA>

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetHeadsUp): display the current burst
 	rate (Mbit/s) in the HUD, along with total number of bytes read.
	
	* TsLogging.c (TsLogBurstRate): [new func] updates internal state
 	to monitor the burst rate over the last n seconds (n=5 by
 	default). This is a global state for the entire application.
  	(TsLogGetNetBurstRate): [new func] returns the current burst rate
 	in units of Mbit/s. This is calculated using the more correct
 	approach of number of bytes streamed into the application over the
 	last n seconds, rather than the previous solution of averaging
 	over the last n tiles that were read.
	(TsLogGetTotalBytesRead): [new func] returns the total number of
 	bytes read by the application since it started
	(TsLogGetTotalTilesRead): [new func] returns the total number of
 	tiles read by the application since it started

	* TerraVision.c (TerraVisionRestartLogging): [new func] sets
 	logging on for all open connections, but only if we are currently
 	logging. Used to refresh the logging characteristics when we load
 	a new dataset and open new connections.
	(TVLoadCallback): refresh the logging state for a connection when
 	we load a dataset. Now you can do things like start logging, then
 	load a dataset, and the dataset will start logging as soon as it
 	loads.

        * TsLogging.c: lots of good changes here. Cleaned up the code a
 	bit. Removed global reference to tsLog - this is now a static
 	variable local to TsLogging.c with interface calls to query/update
 	this structure.
 
	* TVLogger.c (DoubleSeconds): [removed] now exported from
 	TsLogging.c by TsLogging.h

	* Viewpoint.c (ViewpointCycleUp): [new func] flies/jumps to the
 	next bookmark in the viewpoint list for this dataset
	(ViewpointCycleDown): [new func] flies/jumps to the previous
 	bookmark in the viewpoint list for this dataset
 	(ViewpointCountBookmarks): [new func] return the number of
 	bookmarks for the current dataset

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetStartRendering): don't pop up the
 	render widget every time we open the 3-D Viewer.
	(ThreeDWidgetKeypress): further keyboard support for 3-D viewer: R
 	= render settings, N = navigation settings, D = debug settings, P
 	= viewpoint position, B = viewpoint bookmarks, PgUp = fly to next
 	viewpoint, PgDn = fly to previous viewpoint, O = reset to origin,
 	Left/Right/Up/Down = move viewpoint (def=rotate, +shift=slide,
 	+ctrl=zoom).

