Sat Feb 20 12:29:21 1999  Martin Reddy  <reddy@Lomond.AI.SRI.COM>

	* ThreeDWidget1.c (ThreeDWidgetInitView): set the initial view to
	the setting of the Origin bookmark, if one exists. If not, then
	just go to the bottom-left corner of the dataset as we used to do.

	* Viewpoint.c (GetViewpointOrigin): [new func] checks to see if
	there is a bookmark called "Origin" for the current dataset and
	returns it location if so.

	* Viewpoint.c: previously the z and y coordinates were flipped
	(assuming z=up). I have corrected all of these references. In
 	order to maintain backward file compatibility, viewpoint (x,y,z)
 	are stored in the bookmarks file using a "location" field. The
 	previous "position" field, where y and z were flipped, is still
 	read in correctly so old bookmarks will continue to work.

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetUpdate): added new navigation
	mode! If you press a SHIFT key while using the mouse in the 3D
	widget, then you will get a viewer-based movement, e.g. slide
	left/right, slide up/down, move forward/backward along view
	direction. 

	* ThreeDControl.c (ThreeDControlMove): in the Viewpoint Controls,
	the Z buttons moved you along the Y axis and the Y buttons moved
	you along the Z axis. Let's keep things simple and reveal the fact
	that Y = up.

	* Database.c (DBaseInitOpenTV): in the Open Dataset window, make
	the database filename entry widget be the initially selected
	widget so that the user just needs to type and it will directly go
	into the filename string.

	* ThreeDWidget.c (ThreeDWidgetKeyrelease): [new func] detects a
	key release event. Added code to keep track of when the SHIFT and
	CTRL keys are depressed. The static variables shiftDown and
	ctrlDown now track whether either of these keys are currently
	depressed. 

