	* Texture.c: #include <assert.h> (currently disabled).
	(tqueue_callback_t): New type.  Function used for tqueue
	  callbacks.
	(struct tqueue): Add used field, which counts entries in the
	  queue. Add fields for enter and remove callbacks.
	(tqueue_clear): Initialize used field.
	(tqueue_enter_callback): New function.  Registers callback to be
	  called when new entry added.
	(tqueue_remove_callback): New function.  Registers callback to be
	  called when entry is removed from queue.
	(tqueue_empty): Use used == 0 as test.
	(tqueue_full): Use used == size as test.
	(tqueue_used): Just return used count.
	(tqueue_enqueue): Increment used and call enter callback.
	(tqueue_dequeue): Decrement used and call remove callback.
	(tqueue_index_valid): New function.  Checks validity of index.
	(tqueue_reuse): Check index validity before proceeding.  Decrement
	  used and call remove and enter for two handles affected.
	(TextureCacheUnused): New. Encapsulate count of unused handles.
	(TextureCacheUnuse): New. Encapsulate addition of handle to unused
	  queue. 
	(TextureCacheRemoveUnused): New. Encapsulate removal of handle
	  from unused queue.
	(TextureCacheGetUnused): New. Encapsulate the reuse of unused
	  handles.
	(TextureCacheUnusedEnterCB): New. Callback for addition of handle
	  to unused queue.  Uses eqhash to remember index for later
	  resurrection.
	(TextureCacheUnusedRemoveCB): New. Callback for removal of handle
	  from unused queue.  Deletes eqhash entry for handle.
	(TextureCacheCreate): Register enter and remove callbacks to
	  tqueue.
	(TextureCacheHandleForget): Delete.
	(TextureCacheHandleDelete): Roll in functionality from
	  TextureCacheHandleForget().
	(TextureCacheRemoveCB): Lock TextureCache then call
	  TextureCacheHandleDelete() if needed.
	(TextureCacheUsed): New.  Returns number of handles in the cache,
	  equal to the total hash table size minus the number of unused
	  entries, since those are entered twice.
	(TextureCacheHandleCreate): Modify strategy to fill up cache
	  before reusing bound handles.  Should provide much better
	  behavior.  Use TextureCacheGetUnused() to obtain reusable
	  handle.  Add sanity check (disabled by NDEBUG).
	(TextureCacheHandleResurrect): Use TextureCacheRemoveUnused() to
	  restore handle to active status.
	(TextureCacheHandleFree): Use TextureCacheUsed() to check whether
	  handle can be placed on unused queue and TextureCacheUnuse() to
	  do so.  Add sanity check (disabled by NDEBUG).
	(TextureCacheHandleRelease): Add assertion that h->use_count >= 0.
	
