	* Texture.c (struct tqueue): New structure.  Encapsulates the
	  management of currently unused TextureCacheHandles.  Implements
	  a circular array as a queue of unused tiles.
	(tqueue_clear): New.  Clear a tqueue, making it empty.
	(tqueue_init): New.  Initialize a tqueue, allocating the queue
	  array.
	(tqueue_free): New.  Free up memory allocated by a tqueue.
	(tqueue_empty): New.  Returns true if a tqueue is empty.
	(tqueue_full): New.  Returns true if a tqueue is full.
	(tqueue_used): New.  Returns a count of handles in a tqueue.
	(tqueue_enqueue): New.  Add a handle to the end of a tqueue.
	(tqueue_dequeue): New.  Remove the first handle from a tqueue.
	(tqueue_reuse): New.  Remove the handle indexed by i from a
	  tqueue.
	(tqueue_at): New.  Return the handle indexed by i.
	(tqueue_dump): New.  Describe the contents of a tqueue.
	(tqueue_test): New (disabled).  Test the tqueue functions for
	  enqueuing, dequeuing and reusing elements.  Aborts on failure.
	(TextureCacheCreate): Reinsert assignment of TextureCacheRemoveCB
	  as a TILE_DECACHE callback of the TsGeoPyramid.  Initialize
	  tqueue, and dels list for a cache.
	(TextureCacheHandleForget): New.  Forget about a handle without
	  deleting it.  Used by TextureCacheHandleDelete() and
	  TextureCacheHandleCreate() after grabbing an unused handle.
	(TextureCacheHandleDelete): Call TextureCacheHandleForget() to
	  remove from cache.  Add tex_id to dels list rather than deleting
	  directly. 
	(TextureCachePendingDeletes): New.  Actually deletes all of the
	  pending texture object deletion requests generated by
	  TextureCacheHandleDelete().
	(TextureCacheRemoveCB): Fixed up to TextureCacheHandleDelete() if
	  a matching handle is found for the decached tile.
	(TextureCacheHandleCreate): Use tqueue_dequeue() to obtain an
	  unused tile.  Mark such tiles as unmatched so that tex_id will
	  be reused.
	(TextureCacheHandleResurrect): Use tqueue_reuse() to resurrect an
	  unused tile.
	(TextureCacheCountUnused): Deleted.
	(TextureCacheHandleFree): Use tqueue primitives to manage unused
	  tiles.
	(TextureCacheDumpElem): Moved out of TextureCacheDump().
	(TextureCacheDump): Use tqueue_dump() to describe state of unused
	  tiles.  Fix iteration over TextureTraceList.
	(TextureCacheReset): Use tqueue_clear().
	(TextureCacheCheckTextures): New (disabled).  Double checks the
	  status of OpenGL texture objects against the textures in the
	  cache.  Dumps the cache on failure.
	(TextureCacheBindSlow): As this is the only function which is
	  guaranteed to be called inside an OpenGL rendering context, call
	  TextureCachePendingDeletes() to clean up deleted texture
	  objects.  Update min_id and max_id fields of cache.  Marks
	  handle as tex_matched after texture definition is complete. Call
	  TextureCacheCheckTextures() every 128 bindings (disabled).
	(TextureCacheReleaseVisibleList): Clear v->texnode after releasing
	  texture.
	(TextureCachePrepareVisibleList): Trace number of hashed and
	  unused tiles.
	(TextureCacheCheckUnused): New.  Checks validity of the handle of
	  an unused tile.
	(TextureCacheCheckHash): New. Callback for eqhash_forall().
	  Checks the validity of each element in the TextureCache.eqhash
	  table. 
	(TextureCacheCheckVisibleLists): New.  Checks the validity of the
	  TextureCache against the three VisibleLists passed in.  This is
	  only a valid test if these are the *only* three lists sharing
	  this cache.
	* TextureInline.h (TextureTrace): Add tex_id field to
	  TextureTrace.  Tracks which texture id was bound to a handle at
	  the time.
	(struct TextureCache): Remove ad-hoc unused tile values and add a
	  reference to modularized tqueue.  Add min_id and max_id fields
	  which identify the range of texture objects handled by this
	  cache.  Add len_dels, dels and dels_end fields for managing a
	  list of texture objects pending deletion.
	(struct TextureCacheHandle): Add tex_matched bit which is true
	  only when we know that the tex_id matches the tile.  If it is
	  false then the tex_id must be rebound in order to be of use.
	(TextureTraceAdd): Track the value of h->tex_id.
	* ThreeDWidget.c (CreateThreeDWidget): Remove initialization of
	  texture cache and renderPrimitive cache.  Moved to
	  ThreeDWidgetInitializeGraphics().
	(ThreeDWidgetInitializeGraphics): Move texture cache and
	  renderPrimitive cache initialization here, where we are inside a
	  valid OpenGL context.  This ensures that TextureTune() has
	  already been executed.
	* ThreeDWidget1.c (ClearWorkList): Call
	  TextureCacheCheckVisibleLists() every 64 times this is called,
	  and only if minimal texture cache tracing is being done.
	* TwoDWidget.c (CreateTwoDWidget): Remove texture cache
	  initialization.  Move to TwoDWidgetInitCB().
	(TwoDWidgetInitCB): Initialize texture cache here, where we are
	  inside a valid OpenGL context.  This ensures that TextureTune()
	  has already been executed.

	* TwoDWidget.c: #include <pthr/list.h> instead of "list.h"
	(TwoDWidgetGetButtonStates): Don't try to iterate
	  on a non-existent list threeD->linked2DWidgets.

	* Visible.c (poppingStrategy): New variable.  Set to
	  VisiblePopping_LowRes as current default.
	(GenVisibleList1): Implement VisiblePopping_LowRes strategy by
	  separating the identification of leaf nodes (not to be recursed
	  on) from nodes which should be included in a VisibleList.  The
	  LowRes strategy includes a tile in the list unless *all* of its
	  children in the tree are ready.
	* Visible.h (struct VisibleStruct): New field `flags' to describe
	  properties of this visibility primitive (e.g. that it is a
	  lowres tile that has children in the rendered set).
	(VISFLAG_*): New flags for VisibleStruct.flags.
	(enum VisiblePoppingStrategy): Selects a strategy to use to reduce
	  visibility popping (None, LowRes or LowFrag).  Currently only
	  None and LowRes are implemented.
	(poppingStrategy): New variable. Set to popping strategy currently
	  used.

	* configure.in: Allow inclusion and use of conversions library.

